## CLEANUP-2: Split `EventsController` into partial-class files

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
None yet.

### Summary
Split `Controllers/EventsController.cs` (755 lines) into the partial-class structure
`CODING_CONVENTIONS.md` already prescribes by name, with zero behavior change.

### Motivation
`EventsController` is by far the largest file in the codebase and covers several distinguishable
subjects (create/join, sign-in, the event home page, browser-cookie access management).
`CODING_CONVENTIONS.md`'s "Controllers vs. Services" section names the exact target split for this
file as its own worked example, specifically to keep routes, DI registration, and shared private
helpers working with zero behavior change (as opposed to splitting into separate controller
classes, which risks silently changing a URL).

### Proposed Changes
Same class name, marked `partial` in every file, same route attributes, same constructor/DI
(constructor and fields stay in the core file only):

- **`Controllers/EventsController.cs`** (core) — constructor, fields, `EventAccessCookiePrefix`,
  `Create`, `Join`, and the shared private helpers `GetEventAsync`/`CreateEventNotFoundResult`.
- **`Controllers/EventsController.SignIn.cs`** — both `SignIn` overloads,
  `BuildSignInViewModelAsync`, `NormalizeSignInModel`, `ApplySignInViewModelState`,
  `GetSelectedExistingParticipantAsync`, `TryCreateNewParticipantAsync`,
  `TryUpdateExistingParticipantAsync`, `ValidateParticipantUniquenessAsync`, `RequiresRejoinCode`,
  `HasConflictingAccountOwner`, `NormalizeColor`.
- **`Controllers/EventsController.Home.cs`** — `Home`.
- **`Controllers/EventsController.AccessCookie.cs`** — `GetAuthorizedParticipantAsync`,
  `GetCurrentParticipantAsync`, `SetEventAccessCookie`, `GetEventAccessCookieName`.

### Acceptance Criteria
- All existing routes (`EventSignIn` GET/POST, `EventHome` GET, `Create` POST, `Join` POST) resolve
  identically — verified by hitting each one manually.
- `dotnet build` succeeds; no route-attribute duplication or DI registration change needed.
- Manual click-through of the full create → join → sign-in → event home flow behaves identically.
- No method signature or route attribute changes — this is a pure file reorganization.

### Out of Scope
- Any separate controller classes (explicitly rejected per `CODING_CONVENTIONS.md` — risks
  silently changing a URL).
- Any logic change beyond CLEANUP-1's `RequiresRejoinCode` dedup, which should land before this split.

