## CLEANUP-3: Comment-density backfill

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
None yet.

### Summary
Bring doc-comment coverage up to what `CODING_CONVENTIONS.md` calls for — `///` on essentially
every class and on both public and private methods, denser than typical minimal-comment style, and
matching HTML comment density (`<!-- ... -->`) on the view side.

### Motivation
This convention is intentionally the opposite of typical minimal-comment guidance, and the current
codebase has real gaps against it: undocumented constructors/fields on most controllers/services,
systemic use of `//` instead of `///` on nearly every property in `Event.cs`/`Participant.cs`/
`ApplicationUser.cs`, an entirely undocumented `IdentityRoleSeeder.cs`, zero `///` comments
anywhere in `ManageUsers.cshtml.cs` (the single largest gap found), an undocumented
`ApplicationDbContext` class and its seven `DbSet<T>` properties, and three views
(`Home/Privacy.cshtml`, `Shared/Error.cshtml`, `Shared/_Layout.cshtml`) with zero HTML section
comments despite comparable views being heavily commented.

Sequenced after CLEANUP-2 so comments land on `EventsController`'s final split file layout rather
than the monolithic file that's about to be reorganized.

### Proposed Changes
Pattern applied throughout: add a missing class/type `///` summary; add missing `///` method
summaries (public and private alike); convert systemic `//` property comments to proper `///`
`<summary>` blocks; add HTML `<!-- -->` section comments to views currently missing them.

- **Controllers**: `EventsController.*.cs` (post-split) and `MyEventsController.cs` — document
  fields/constructors; fix `MyEventsController`'s inconsistent doc style between `Index` (empty
  `<param>`/`<returns>` tags) and `Delete` (no tags at all). `HomeController.cs` is already fully
  compliant — no change needed.
- **Services**: `UniqueCodeGenerator.cs` — document the constructor and the private
  `GenerateUniqueCodeAsync`.
- **Models**: `Event.cs`, `Participant.cs`, `ApplicationUser.cs` — convert `//` to `///` on
  properties, document private consts and `Id` properties, add `EventSettings`'s missing class
  summary. Document `IdentityConfiguration.Configure` and all of `IdentityRoleSeeder.cs`.
- **Data**: `ApplicationDbContext.cs` — document the class and each of the seven `DbSet<T>`
  properties individually (replacing the single collective `//` comment).
- **Razor Pages**: `Areas/Admin/Pages/Users/ManageUsers.cshtml.cs` — document the class,
  constructor, and all six methods.
- **Views**: `Home/Privacy.cshtml`, `Shared/Error.cshtml`, `Shared/_Layout.cshtml` — add HTML
  section comments matching `Home/Index.cshtml`'s and `MyEvents/Index.cshtml`'s density.

### Acceptance Criteria
- `dotnet build` succeeds with no new warnings.
- Every class/type in the touched files has a `///` summary; every public and private method has one.
- No logic, signature, or markup structure changes — comments only.

### Out of Scope
- Any code/logic changes (that's CLEANUP-1/CLEANUP-2/CLEANUP-4).
- Comment backfill on files not listed above, if any were missed in review — flag separately rather
  than expanding this entry's scope mid-implementation.

