## CLEANUP-4: View/JS consistency fixes

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
None yet.

### Summary
Bring `Events/SignIn.cshtml`'s inline script in line with the established
`Views/MyEvents/Index.cshtml` reference pattern, and clean up a couple of small dead-CSS/magic-number
inconsistencies elsewhere.

### Motivation
`CODING_CONVENTIONS.md` specifies vanilla JS in an IIFE per view, with every queried element
null-guarded before wiring listeners — `MyEvents/Index.cshtml` follows this correctly and is the
named reference; `SignIn.cshtml` is the only other view with real inline script logic, and follows
neither part of the pattern (no IIFE wrapper; only 1 of ~7 queried elements is guarded). Separately,
`Home/Index.cshtml` hardcodes `maxlength="6"` where `SignIn.cshtml` already correctly references
`ModelConstants.UniqueCodeLength` for the equivalent field, and has two CSS classes
(`create-event-container`, `join-event-container`) confirmed unstyled anywhere in the project.
`Program.cs` has a stale comment referencing a type name (`EventCodeGenerator`) that was renamed to
`UniqueCodeGenerator`, plus mixed tabs/spaces indentation.

### Proposed Changes
- **`Views/Events/SignIn.cshtml`** — wrap the script body in an IIFE; add a null-guard on every
  queried element before wiring its listener(s), matching `MyEvents/Index.cshtml`'s pattern.
- **`Views/Home/Index.cshtml`** — replace `maxlength="6"` with
  `@WhenWorksWeb.Common.ModelConstants.UniqueCodeLength`; remove the unstyled
  `create-event-container`/`join-event-container` CSS classes (confirm with the developer first if
  styling was actually intended for these rather than dropping them).
- **`Program.cs`** — fix the stale "EventCodeGenerator" comment to say `UniqueCodeGenerator`;
  normalize mixed tabs/spaces indentation to match `.editorconfig`.
- Optional/low priority: `Views/MyEvents/Index.cshtml`'s `.selected` CSS class has no stylesheet
  rule behind it (toggled but has no visible effect) — either add a style or drop the toggle;
  `Views/Shared/_LoginPartial.cshtml` has a few double-space attribute typos.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Sign-in page behaves identically for all flows (new participant, existing participant, rejoin
  code) with no JS console errors, verified manually in a browser.
- No element-not-found script errors on any page state (e.g. rejoin code input hidden/shown).
- `dotnet build` succeeds; no markup/route changes.

### Out of Scope
- Any change to `Views/MyEvents/Index.cshtml`'s already-compliant IIFE/JSON pattern beyond the
  optional `.selected` note above.
- Any new CSS framework, shared JS bundle, or build tooling — the project deliberately stays with
  per-view vanilla JS and direct Bootstrap utility classes.
